# Code Review Gate

Before a git milestone, review the change with the reviewer skill. Do not commit, push, or open a PR until the required tier passed or the user explicitly skips review.

| Milestone | Skill | Reviewer tier |
|---|---|---|
| Commit | `skills/ci-commit/SKILL.md` | change |
| Open PR | `skills/ci-pr/SKILL.md` | pr |
| Push | `skills/ci-push/SKILL.md` | pr |

The reviewer is `skills/reviewer/SKILL.md`. For an iterative fix-until-clean pass, use `skills/ci-local-review-loop/SKILL.md`. For an autonomous PR review→fix loop, use `skills/ci-pr-review-loop/SKILL.md`.

## Consent and skipping

- Commit needs explicit consent (`git-commit-consent.mdc`); push needs explicit consent (`git-push-consent.mdc`).
- If the user explicitly skips review, proceed but state that review was skipped.
- If the repo provides the review-lock helper, the CI skills may use it to skip a redundant scan when the tree is unchanged. It is advisory only — never a substitute for reviewing changed code, never a blocker when absent.

## Skip conditions

- No uncommitted changes → change tier is trivially clean.
- No branch diff vs the base → pr tier is trivially clean.
